<title>UK: OPEC says sees demand on crude in '97 at 25.2 mbpd.</title>
<headline>OPEC says sees demand on crude in '97 at 25.2 mbpd.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>OPEC's Vienna Secretariat revised higher its forecast for world demand on OPEC crude this year by 100,000 barrels per day (bpd) to 25.2 million bpd, OPEC news agency said.</p>
<p>In a monthly report the Secretariat also said OPEC production in December, according to member countries, was at 24.66 million bpd, down from 24.69 million in November.</p>
<p>A Reuter survey of December OPEC output put production at 26.4 million.</p>
<p>The report also revised higher OPEC's estimate for world demand this year by 50,000 bpd to 70.84 million.</p>
<p>-- Richard Mably, London newsroom +44 171 542 8060</p>
